IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er6-nouns`
IMPORT `er6-schedule-i-regions`

-- Tests of er6-schedule-i-regions. Expected values come from reading Schedule I (SOR-96-332.txt lines 1758-1926):
--   * the first group is generated from the lists the Schedule gives: for every limb of every region, a place that has what
--     the limb requires is in that region and in no other; and for every "not part of" limb, a place that has the excluded
--     part is not in that region. Census division numbers and subdivision numbers that the limb does not mention are 0,
--     which is no real number, so another region cannot claim the place by accident;
--   * the second group is written by hand from the sentences of the Schedule that need a human to read them: the portions,
--     the split of Census Division No. 34 east of London, Ottawa on one side of the river and Hull on the other, and the
--     census subdivisions of Newfoundland.

§ `test helpers`

GIVEN province IS AN `er6 Province or territory`
      cd IS A NUMBER
      csd IS A NUMBER
      cma IS AN `er6 Census Metropolitan Area or none`
      ca IS AN `er6 Census Agglomeration or none`
      east IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `er6 Place`
`er6 test place` province cd csd cma ca east MEANS
    `er6 Place` WITH
        `province or territory` IS province
        `census division` IS cd
        `census subdivision` IS csd
        `census metropolitan area` IS cma
        `census agglomeration` IS ca
        `east of the Census Metropolitan Area of London` IS east

-- How many of the 62 regions the place is in: the Schedule's regions must not overlap, so this is 1 for a place in Canada
-- that the Schedule covers and 0 for one it does not.
GIVEN place IS A `er6 Place`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `er6 test number of Schedule I regions the place is in` IS
    sum (map (GIVEN b YIELD IF b THEN 1 ELSE 0) (LIST
        `Regs Sch I s 2(1) the place is in the region of Ottawa` place
      , `Regs Sch I s 2(1.1) the place is in the region of Kingston` place
      , `Regs Sch I s 2(1.2) the place is in the region of Central Ontario` place
      , `Regs Sch I s 2(2) the place is in the region of Eastern Ontario` place
      , `Regs Sch I s 2(3) the place is in the region of Northern Ontario` place
      , `Regs Sch I s 2(4) the place is in the region of Oshawa` place
      , `Regs Sch I s 2(5) the place is in the region of Toronto` place
      , `Regs Sch I s 2(6) the place is in the region of Hamilton` place
      , `Regs Sch I s 2(7) the place is in the region of St. Catharines` place
      , `Regs Sch I s 2(8) the place is in the region of London` place
      , `Regs Sch I s 2(9) the place is in the region of Niagara` place
      , `Regs Sch I s 2(10) the place is in the region of Windsor` place
      , `Regs Sch I s 2(11) the place is in the region of Kitchener` place
      , `Regs Sch I s 2(12) the place is in the region of Huron` place
      , `Regs Sch I s 2(13) the place is in the region of South Central Ontario` place
      , `Regs Sch I s 2(14) the place is in the region of Sudbury` place
      , `Regs Sch I s 2(15) the place is in the region of Thunder Bay` place
      , `Regs Sch I s 3(1) the place is in the region of Gaspésie-Îles-de-la-Madeleine` place
      , `Regs Sch I s 3(2) the place is in the region of Quebec` place
      , `Regs Sch I s 3(3) the place is in the region of Central Quebec` place
      , `Regs Sch I s 3(4) the place is in the region of Trois-Rivières` place
