#ASSERT `er6 test number of Schedule I regions the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Nunavut` 0 0 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch I s 14(2) the place is in the region of Nunavut` (`er6 test place` `er6 Nunavut` 0 6204003 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE))

§ `written by hand from the sentences of Schedule I`

-- s 1: which edition of Statistics Canada's classification defines each term for a section.
-- "Census Agglomeration for the purposes of sections 2, 5, 7 and 9 ... SGC 1996 and for the purposes of sections 8, 12 and 13 ... SGC 2011"
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I s 1 the edition that defines Census Agglomeration in section` 2 EQUALS JUST `er6 SGC 1996`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I s 1 the edition that defines Census Agglomeration in section` 5 EQUALS JUST `er6 SGC 1996`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I s 1 the edition that defines Census Agglomeration in section` 7 EQUALS JUST `er6 SGC 1996`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I s 1 the edition that defines Census Agglomeration in section` 9 EQUALS JUST `er6 SGC 1996`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I s 1 the edition that defines Census Agglomeration in section` 8 EQUALS JUST `er6 SGC 2011`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I s 1 the edition that defines Census Agglomeration in section` 12 EQUALS JUST `er6 SGC 2011`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I s 1 the edition that defines Census Agglomeration in section` 13 EQUALS JUST `er6 SGC 2011`
-- s 3 mentions no agglomeration, so the definition says nothing for it: the text does not answer.
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I s 1 the edition that defines Census Agglomeration in section` 3 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I s 1 the edition that defines Census Agglomeration in section` 14 EQUALS NOTHING
-- "Census Subdivision for the purposes of sections 5 and 11 ... 1996 and for the purposes of sections 8 and 12 to 14 ... 2011"
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I s 1 the edition that defines Census Subdivision in section` 5 EQUALS JUST `er6 SGC 1996`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I s 1 the edition that defines Census Subdivision in section` 11 EQUALS JUST `er6 SGC 1996`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I s 1 the edition that defines Census Subdivision in section` 8 EQUALS JUST `er6 SGC 2011`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I s 1 the edition that defines Census Subdivision in section` 12 EQUALS JUST `er6 SGC 2011`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I s 1 the edition that defines Census Subdivision in section` 13 EQUALS JUST `er6 SGC 2011`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I s 1 the edition that defines Census Subdivision in section` 14 EQUALS JUST `er6 SGC 2011`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I s 1 the edition that defines Census Subdivision in section` 2 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I s 1 the edition that defines Census Subdivision in section` 10 EQUALS NOTHING
-- "Census Division ... SGC 1996" and "Census Metropolitan Area ... SGC 1996" for the whole Schedule
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I s 1 the edition that defines Census Division` EQUALS `er6 SGC 1996`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I s 1 the edition that defines Census Metropolitan Area` EQUALS `er6 SGC 1996`

-- The helper behind "Census Division Nos. 12 to 16": the whole numbers from 12 to 16, both ends included.
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I whole numbers from` 12 `to` 16 EQUALS LIST 12, 13, 14, 15, 16
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I whole numbers from` 14 `to` 18 EQUALS LIST 14, 15, 16, 17, 18
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I whole numbers from` 5 `to` 5 EQUALS LIST 5
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I whole numbers from` 6 `to` 5 EQUALS EMPTY

-- Ottawa and Hull are the two sides of one metropolitan area: s 2(1) takes the part in Ontario, s 3(10) the part in Quebec.
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Ontario` 0 0 `er6 Ottawa — Hull CMA` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Ottawa`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Quebec` 0 0 `er6 Ottawa — Hull CMA` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Hull`
-- s 3(3)(e): Census Division No. 82 of Quebec outside the metropolitan area is Central Quebec; inside it, Hull.
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Quebec` 82 0 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Central Quebec`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Quebec` 82 0 `er6 Ottawa — Hull CMA` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Hull`

-- Census division numbers repeat from province to province: Census Division No. 11 is in Central Ontario only in Ontario
-- (s 2(1.2)(a)); in Alberta it is part of Southern Alberta (s 10(3)(b)).
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Ontario` 11 0 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Central Ontario`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Alberta` 11 0 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Southern Alberta`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Alberta` 11 0 `er6 Edmonton CMA` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Edmonton`
-- Census Division No. 11 in Ontario inside the Kingston agglomeration is Kingston (s 2(1.1)), not Central Ontario.
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Ontario` 11 0 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 Kingston CA` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Kingston`

-- s 2(1.2)(b) and (9)(a): a division that contains a metropolitan area is that region where the place is in the area and the
-- rest of the division belongs to another.
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Ontario` 18 0 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Central Ontario`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Ontario` 18 0 `er6 Oshawa CMA` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Oshawa`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Ontario` 18 0 `er6 Toronto CMA` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Toronto`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Ontario` 26 0 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Niagara`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Ontario` 26 0 `er6 Hamilton CMA` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Hamilton`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Ontario` 26 0 `er6 St. Catharines — Niagara CMA` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of St. Catharines`

-- s 2(9)(b) and (12)(a): Census Division No. 34 outside London is Niagara where it "lies east of" London, Huron where it does not.
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Ontario` 34 0 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` TRUE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Niagara`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Ontario` 34 0 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Huron`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Ontario` 34 0 `er6 London CMA` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` TRUE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of London`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Ontario` 34 0 `er6 London CMA` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of London`

-- New Brunswick, s 5: Census Division No. 2 is split by the Saint John metropolitan area, No. 6 by the Moncton agglomeration.
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 New Brunswick` 2 0 `er6 Saint John CMA` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Fredericton — Moncton — Saint John`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 New Brunswick` 2 0 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Madawaska — Charlotte`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 New Brunswick` 6 0 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 Moncton CA` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Fredericton — Moncton — Saint John`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 New Brunswick` 6 0 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Restigouche — Albert`
-- New Brunswick census subdivisions: 1303001 (s 5(1)(c)), 1303014 (s 5(3)(b)), 1310004 (s 5(2)(c)) and 1310036 (s 5(3)(f)).
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 New Brunswick` 3 1303001 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Fredericton — Moncton — Saint John`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 New Brunswick` 3 1303014 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Restigouche — Albert`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 New Brunswick` 10 1310004 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Madawaska — Charlotte`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 New Brunswick` 10 1310036 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Restigouche — Albert`

-- Newfoundland, s 11: two census subdivisions of Census Division No. 1 lie in the St. John's metropolitan area but belong to Newfoundland/Labrador.
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Newfoundland` 1 1500 `er6 St. John’s CMA` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of St. John’s`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Newfoundland` 1 1557 `er6 St. John’s CMA` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Newfoundland/Labrador`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Newfoundland` 1 1559 `er6 St. John’s CMA` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Newfoundland/Labrador`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Newfoundland` 1 1200 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Newfoundland/Labrador`

-- Saskatchewan, s 9: Census Division No. 12 is split three ways.
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Saskatchewan` 12 0 `er6 Saskatoon CMA` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Saskatoon`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Saskatchewan` 12 0 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 North Battleford CA` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Northern Saskatchewan`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Saskatchewan` 12 0 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Southern Saskatchewan`

-- British Columbia s 7(4)(b) and (4.1): Census Division No. 9 outside the Abbotsford agglomeration is Southern Coastal.
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 British Columbia` 9 0 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 Abbotsford CA` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Abbotsford`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 British Columbia` 9 0 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Southern Coastal British Columbia`

