#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Northwest Territories` 0 0 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 Yellowknife CA` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Yellowknife`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Northwest Territories` 0 0 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of the Northwest Territories`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Nunavut` 6204 6204003 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Iqaluit`
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Nunavut` 6204 6204004 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Nunavut`
-- The territory test matters: the same agglomeration facts in the wrong province give no region of that name.
#ASSERT `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` (`er6 test place` `er6 Ontario` 0 0 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 Whitehorse CA` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

